For explicit task scope:

```bash
mkdir -p governance/task-scopes
ak task scope export <TASK-ID> > governance/task-scopes/AK-<TASK-ID>.snapshot.json
./scripts/check-task-scope-snapshots.sh
```

`AK_CMD="${AK_CMD:-ak}"` may select an explicit compatible executable. Missing required AK access fails closed; do not substitute a hand-authored state store.

## Reusable procedures

Reusable cognitive and operating procedures are discovered through Prompt Vault query/retrieve surfaces. Check the template's dispatch posture before execution. Keep runtime decisions and evidence in AK rather than copying reusable procedure bodies into this repository.

## Engineering contract

If this agent ships language-specific software, adopt the matching engineering-core lane through `policy/engineering-lane.json` and record local deltas in `docs/engineering.local.md`. Otherwise use engineering-core catalog/list commands for guidance without pretending a local lane contract exists.

## Validation

```bash
./scripts/ci/smoke.sh
./scripts/ci/full.sh
```

Full CI validates the AK projection when the repo is registered, checks task-scope snapshots, and runs ROCS validation when ontology artifacts exist.

## Customization

- `repo_slug`: agent product identifier;
- `agent_owner_handle`: CODEOWNERS entry for agent-owned paths;
- `core_owner_handle`: CODEOWNERS entry for core paths;
- `enable_vouch_gate`, `enable_community_pack`, `enable_release_pack`: optional profile metadata.

## ROCS command flow

```bash
./scripts/rocs.sh --doctor
./scripts/rocs.sh --which
```

If ontology artifacts exist, validate through the same wrapper.

## Knowledge evolution

Capture raw sessions in `diary/`, crystallize owner-local patterns in `docs/learnings/`, route reusable procedures to Prompt Vault, and route semantic changes to their ontology owner.
